Source/wheel installs resolve Python dependencies separately. Desktop packages
bundle them and include their installed license texts under licenses/:

  construct     MIT           binary parsing of export.pdb
  pyrekordbox   MIT           ANLZ tag structures
  click         BSD-3-Clause  command-line interface
  rich          MIT           human-readable output
  numpy         BSD-3-Clause  waveform processing
  pywebview     BSD-3-Clause  optional desktop UI
  onnxruntime   MIT           optional offline grid repair inference
  BeatThis      MIT           small0 weights and adapted pre/postprocessing

mutagen (GPL-2.0-or-later) is a DEVELOPMENT dependency only. It is used
exclusively in the test suite as an independent oracle confirming that
`src/rb2engine/reader/tags.py` extracts byte-identical cover art. It is not
imported by any module under `src/`, is not required at runtime, and is not
included in release artifacts.

BeatThis model and inference
---------------------------
The optional grid repair component redistributes the MIT-licensed small0 model
from CPJKU/beat_this 1.1.0, exported to ONNX. Its NumPy pre/postprocessing adapts
the upstream implementation. The upstream license is included in
src/rb2engine/gridrepair/assets/LICENSE and desktop licenses/BeatThis/LICENSE.
The model source URL, checkpoint hash and exported file hashes are recorded in
assets/manifest.json. Model inference is offline; PyTorch is not bundled.
  https://github.com/CPJKU/beat_this

FFmpeg runtime
--------------
Source/wheel waveform generation executes separately installed ffmpeg/ffprobe.
The project's AAC helper source compiles locally and dynamically links the
user's libavformat, libavcodec and libavutil. These libraries are real runtime
dependencies, not merely format references. No FFmpeg source, binary, linked
helper binary, Engine private library or commercial audio is shipped in this
project's source archive or wheel.

FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later by default, with optional GPL components that change
the license of a configured build. The installed build determines the applicable
terms; the MIT license for this project's source does not relicense FFmpeg.
Redistributing a compiled helper or FFmpeg libraries requires examining that
build's terms, notices and corresponding-source obligations. See:
  https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

Desktop distributions bundle a minimal FFmpeg 8.0.3 build with GPL, nonfree,
networking and external codec components disabled. The AAC helper dynamically
links its replaceable LGPL libraries. The complete FFmpeg source tarball,
LGPLv2.1 text, exact configuration, helper source and build script are included
under licenses/FFmpeg in each desktop archive. No Engine private library or
commercial audio is included. Windows GCC support libraries, when included,
retain their respective runtime-exception/license notices under licenses/.

The projects below informed this work but are NOT included, copied, linked
against, or redistributed here. They are credited because interoperability
work is only possible thanks to the people who documented these formats.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
crate-digger — Deep Symmetry, LLC and contributors (EPL-2.0)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  https://github.com/Deep-Symmetry/crate-digger

crate-digger's Kaitai Struct definition `rekordbox_pdb.ksy` is the reference
reverse-engineering of the rekordbox `export.pdb` DeviceSQL format. It was
read as documentation while writing `src/rb2engine/reader/pdb.py`.

No crate-digger source is included, and no code is generated from its
`.ksy`. The parser here is an independent implementation written against the
MIT-licensed `construct` library. Facts about a binary layout — field order,
offsets, endianness — are not copyrightable expression, and none of
crate-digger's code or text is reproduced.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
libdjinterop — xsco and contributors (LGPL-3.0)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  https://github.com/xsco/libdjinterop

libdjinterop is the reference for the Engine DJ SQLite schema and the
PerformanceData blob encodings. It was read as documentation only.

No libdjinterop source code, header, object code, or linked binary is
included in, generated into, or linked against rb2engine. Critically, the
schema DDL committed under `src/rb2engine/writer/ddl/` was NOT transcribed
from libdjinterop: it is captured with `sqlite3` from databases that Engine
DJ itself authored, so the schema text originates from Engine's own output.

